# Pending human-applied patch — issue #841
#
# WHAT: drops the "predecessor-project-style" private-repo framing from the
#       `reviewer.mode: different-model-codex` comment in the live root config. Keeps the
#       real point (this mode is gate② run as a fresh non-author hosted Codex review). No
#       behavior change — comment-only.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS: #841 (public-launch hygiene) scrubs references to the project's private
#       predecessor from production code and user-facing docs — a user browsing the shipped
#       repo has no access to that private repo, and a comment pointing at it only confuses.
#       See #841's PR body for the full file-by-file classification table.
#
# WHY IT IS A PATCH AND NOT A COMMIT: `sapwood.config.yaml` is human-merge-only, the WHOLE
#       file, no per-field carve-out (docs/security.md "Human-merge-only paths") — enforced
#       by the guard, not by convention. An autonomous worker's write to it is denied at the
#       tool level.
#
# APPLY (from the repo root), then delete this file:
#       git apply docs/patches/841-sapwood-config-archaeology-scrub.patch
#       git rm docs/patches/841-sapwood-config-archaeology-scrub.patch
#
